<%- include("../partials/head",{metaTitle}) %><main id="main"><section class="page-hero page-hero--compact"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Community policy</span><h1>Terms and Content Policy</h1><p>Guidelines for using ThaiGame.org's game pages, creator profiles, videos, links, and community events.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container legal"><h2>1. ThaiGame.org's role</h2><p>ThaiGame.org is a public information and promotional directory. It is not a store, publisher, distributor, or game-file hosting service. Purchases, downloads, payments, and services happen on external websites chosen by each creator.</p><h2>2. Rights to content</h2><p>Posters must have the right to use all text, images, trademarks, videos, links, and information they submit. Copying, impersonation, misleading claims, or unauthorized use of someone else's intellectual property is not allowed.</p><h2>3. AI disclosure</h2><p>If AI was used in meaningful parts of a game, such as art, audio, code, dialogue, music, marketing copy, or other assets, creators should disclose those areas so players, event organizers, and stakeholders can evaluate the work transparently.</p><h2>4. Prohibited content</h2><p>Illegal content, malware, illegal gambling, pornography, harassment, hate, deceptive links, copyright-infringing files, and content that may harm users or rights holders are not allowed.</p><h2>5. Moderation</h2><p>Administrators may hide, remove, request edits to, or suspend games, events, profiles, and accounts when there are safety, copyright, accuracy, or misuse concerns.</p><h2>6. Privacy</h2><p>When a profile is public, details such as email, LINE ID, phone number, bio, and social links may be visible on the internet. Users should only publish information they are comfortable making public.</p><h2>7. Cookies and sessions</h2><p>The site uses necessary cookies for login, security, and CSRF protection. ThaiGame.org does not host game files or payment flows.</p><h2>8. Reporting issues</h2><p>To report rights violations, inappropriate content, or incorrect information, contact the administrator with the page URL, brief evidence, and a return contact channel. Content may be hidden while a report is reviewed.</p></div></section></main><%- include("../partials/footer") %>
